# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local dev.
#
# The authority's origin. LEAVE THIS UNSET — it is an override, not a
# setting, and every checked-in configuration omits it.
#
# The API is same-origin with the shell by decision (ADR-0006/0008:
# `connect-src 'self'`, no CORS anywhere), so the correct value is always
# the bundle's own origin, and `src/worker/core.worker.ts` reads that from
# `self.location.origin` at runtime rather than baking it in. In production
# a Worker route puts `hb.twinion.net/api/*` on the authority worker
# (`server/worker/wrangler.toml`); under `vite dev` the dev-server proxy in
# `vite.config.ts` forwards `/api` to `wrangler dev` on 127.0.0.1:8787.
#
# Set it only to point a bundle at an authority that is deliberately NOT its
# own origin — a staging Durable Object, a second workspace. Doing so is a
# cross-origin request the authority will not answer without a CORS lane
# that does not exist, so it also needs a proxy in front of it.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
